{"id":"4A","title":"Law of the Land","part":{"n":4,"title":"Law and Justice"},"url":"/law/04-law-and-justice/4a","entries":[{"id":"4A.1","text":"The laws, statutes, commandments and judgments of God are to be kept throughout the land.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":18,"verses":"4-5"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":5,"verses":"32-33"},{"book":"Ezekiel","chapter":20,"verses":"19"}],"citation":"Lev. 18:4-5; Deut. 5:32-33; Ezek. 20:19."},{"id":"4A.2","text":"There is to be one law applied to the citizen and the stranger.","refs":[{"book":"Exodus","chapter":12,"verses":"49"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":24,"verses":"22"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":9,"verses":"14"}],"citation":"Exod. 12:49; Lev. 24:22; Num. 9:14."},{"id":"4A.3","text":"Foreigners to abide by and obey God's law.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":16,"verses":"29"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":17,"verses":"12-15"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":18,"verses":"26"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":24,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":25,"verses":"6"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":15,"verses":"30"},{"book":"Numbers","chapter":35,"verses":"15"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":1,"verses":"16"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":5,"verses":"14"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":24,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":27,"verses":"19"},{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":31,"verses":"12"},{"book":"Joshua","chapter":8,"verses":"33-35"}],"citation":"Lev. 16:29; Lev. 17:12-15; Lev. 18:26; Lev. 24:16; Lev. 25:6; Num. 15:30; Num. 35:15; Deut. 1:16; Deut. 5:14; Deut. 24:17; Deut. 27:19; Deut. 31:12: Josh. 8:33-35."},{"id":"4A.4","text":"The LORD is our lawgiver.","refs":[{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":33,"verses":"22"},{"book":"James","chapter":4,"verses":"12"}],"citation":"Isa. 33:22; James 4:12."},{"id":"4A.5","text":"You shall not follow the laws and ordinances of other nations in your land.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":18,"verses":"3"},{"book":"Micah","chapter":6,"verses":"16"},{"book":"2 Kings","chapter":17,"verses":"19-20"}],"citation":"Lev. 18:3; Mic. 6:16; 2 Kings 17:19-20."},{"id":"4A.6","text":"He who does any thing defiantly and with contempt for the law, that person shall be cut off from among his people.","refs":[{"book":"Numbers","chapter":15,"verses":"29-31"}],"citation":"Num. 15:29-31."},{"id":"4A.7","text":"All must confirm the words of the law by doing them.","refs":[{"book":"Deuteronomy","chapter":27,"verses":"26"},{"book":"Galatians","chapter":3,"verses":"10"}],"citation":"Deut 27:26; Gal. 3:10."},{"id":"4A.8","text":"Laws and decrees that are contrary to Divine law or justice, or oppress the rights of persons, are repugnant and void.","refs":[{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":10,"verses":"1-2"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":24,"verses":"5-6"},{"book":"Daniel","chapter":3,"verses":"10-30"},{"book":"Daniel","chapter":6,"verses":"5-22"}],"citation":"Isa. 10:1-2; Isa. 24:5-6; Dan. 3:10-30; Dan. 6:5-22."},{"id":"4A.9","text":"We are to remember the ancient events and principles of the past which formed the law of the land.","refs":[{"book":"1 Samuel","chapter":24,"verses":"13"},{"book":"Job","chapter":8,"verses":"8"},{"book":"Isaiah","chapter":51,"verses":"2"},{"book":"Jeremiah","chapter":18,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"1 Sam. 24:13; Job 8:8; Isa. 51:2; Jer. 18:15."}]}